% Call-graph reachability, whole project. The closure is quadratic and the
% constant is the call graph's own density: tsdl's 5k edges derived 173k pairs
% in ~12 s, and VS Code's `vs/base` — 14k functions, 178k edges — takes **38 s
% and 4.1 GB**, which is the most expensive thing in this library by both
% measures. **Ask `orient.dl` for the call-site count first**; at tens of
% thousands, import `callreach_seeded.dl` instead and name the functions the
% question is about.
%
%   reaches(A, B)   a chain of call_edge leads from A to B
%   recursive(F)    F can reach itself (direct or mutual recursion)
%   mutual(A, B)    A and B are distinct and each reaches the other — anchored
%                   on a direct edge, which is ~10x cheaper than joining the
%                   closure with itself

import "callgraph.dl".

reaches(A, B) :- call_edge(A, B).
reaches(A, C) :- call_edge(A, B), reaches(B, C).

recursive(F) :- reaches(F, F).
mutual(A, B) :- call_edge(A, B), reaches(B, A), A != B.
